# PILOT: does learner C learn to STOP at the goal if arrival requires it? (user 2026-11-13 "proceed",
# after the mapping session confirmed the slow-arrival rule is the project's existing knob.)
# = slurm/cluster_frl_c0emb_4towns_ar2_xp_2m_par_resume_2gpu.env (4 towns in parallel on 2 L40s, batched
# critic, pinned expert replay, everything else identical) with ONE reward change:
#   GOAL_ARRIVAL_MAX_SPEED=10 -- arrival inside the 1 m circle counts only at <= 10 km/h. This is
#   v52_reward.env's own value (the chain's slurm/sac_scratch_2t_u5_orterm_idle_nb.env had set it to 0
#   after the user's 2026-11-09 "any speed" decision); src/vae_nav/gated_reward._stopped_enough checks
#   info["speed_kmh"] at the step arrival is tested, so braking inside the circle counts.
# Resumed from the run's 750k checkpoint (its best: 44/80) and run to 850k = a ~100k-step, ~3 h pilot.
# WHY A PILOT, not a 2-day run: the recorded cause of this arm's earlier collapses is that the critic
# credits the expert's braking approach for the +100 arrival bonus, so making braking a CONDITION of that
# bonus pushes on the same machinery. 100k steps is enough to see braking appear or the critic collapse.
# The in-job evals stay ANY-SPEED (slurm/il_eval_val_chw_jr_any1m_ar2.env) so every number stays
# comparable with 250k/500k/750k; the <= 10 km/h column is re-scored offline from each episode's
# min_speed_inside_kmh in eval.json, which needs no GPU.
. "$REPO/slurm/cluster_frl_c0emb_4towns_ar2_xp_2m_par_resume_2gpu.env"
export GOAL_ARRIVAL_MAX_SPEED=10
export FRL_MAX_STEPS=850000
